    "body": "### Summary\n\nWhen `WeightChecker._reset_tensors` executes, it resets model parameters and non-whitelisted buffers. In M-RoPE models (e.g. Qwen3.5-VL), `MRotaryEmbedding` registers `axis_map` as a non-persistent `int64` buffer indicating temporal/height/width rotary lane indexing.\n\nBecause `axis_map` was omitted from `_NON_PERSISTENT_BUFFER_PATTERNS`, `reset_tensors` overwrites the buffer with random `int64` values. Subsequent weight update checks or kernel executions using `axis_map` fail or encounter memory corruption as lane indices diverge outside `{0, 1, 2}`.\n\n### Changes\n\n1. **`python/sglang/srt/utils/weight_checker.py`**:\n   - Added `\"axis_map\"` to `_NON_PERSISTENT_BUFFER_PATTERNS` so `_is_non_persistent_buffer_name()` preserves the buffer across resets and excludes it from parameter checksum mismatches.\n2. **`test/registered/unit/utils/test_weight_checker.py`**:\n   - Registered `rotary_emb_axis_map` in `_TinyModel`.\n   - Added `test_skips_axis_map` in `TestResetTensors` verifying the buffer is untouched during `_reset_tensors()`.\n   - Added `test_matches_axis_map_substring` in `TestIsNonPersistentBufferName`.\n   - Verified snapshot capturing and non-persistent checksum filtering.\n\nFixes #44501\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #39045843564](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39045843564)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #39045843568](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39045843568)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #39045843539](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39045843539)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
